{"diagnosis": "mem_la_addr low bits are 2'b10 instead of 2'b00, so every lookahead fetch/data address is misaligned and the bench reports fetch misalign addr low bits nonzero with FAIL 0xdead. Expected word-aligned {..,2'b00} for both the next_pc fetch path and reg_op1 data path. Root cause is line 382 which hard-codes 2'b10 in both branches of mem_la_addr.", "patch_diff": "diff --git a/picorv32.v b/picorv32.v
--- a/picorv32.v
+++ b/picorv32.v
@@ -382,1 +382,1 @@
-	assign mem_la_addr = (mem_do_prefetch || mem_do_rinst) ? {next_pc[31:2] + mem_la_firstword_xfer, 2'b10} : {reg_op1[31:2], 2'b10};
+	assign mem_la_addr = (mem_do_prefetch || mem_do_rinst) ? {next_pc[31:2] + mem_la_firstword_xfer, 2'b00} : {reg_op1[31:2], 2'b00};", "expected": "tohost PASS (not FAIL 0xdead), no fetch misalign trap, fetch alignment check passes"}

